# Build-context exclusions.
#
# Without this file the context handed to `docker build` includes .venv (460
# MB), .git and every tool cache -- uploaded to the daemon on EVERY build,
# and on a RunPod deployment that context crosses a home uplink.
#
# Mirrors .gitignore where the reasons coincide, and adds the things git
# tracks but an image must never carry: .env (secrets) and tests/.

# ⚠️ The `**/` prefix is load-bearing. A .dockerignore pattern is matched
# against the path relative to the CONTEXT ROOT and `*` does not cross `/`,
# so a bare `__pycache__/` excludes exactly one directory -- the one at the
# root -- and lets the other 98 under src/ ride along into `COPY src/`.
.venv/
venv/
.git/
.github/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/

.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.import_linter_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ⚠️ Secrets. The image must receive its configuration from the environment,
# never from a baked file.
.env
*.local

# Development TLS material -- regenerated per deployment.
deploy/nginx/certs/

build/
dist/
*.log
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
